<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- A round-trip case: this source is built to PDF, the PDF is transcribed, and the     -->
<!-- transcription is compared with this source.  Written for the purpose; nothing here -->
<!-- is taken from any publication.  Exercises: a table with a header row and aligned   -->
<!-- columns, a table holding mathematics, nested lists, a description list, and        -->
<!-- references to tables and to list items.                                            -->
<pretext xml:lang="en-US">
    <docinfo>
        <macros>
        </macros>
    </docinfo>

    <article xml:id="article-small-cases">
        <title>Small cases, tabulated</title>

        <frontmatter>
            <bibinfo>
                <author>
                    <personname>Example Author</personname>
                    <institution>Department of Examples, University of Somewhere</institution>
                </author>
            </bibinfo>
            <titlepage>
                <titlepage-items/>
            </titlepage>
            <abstract>
                <p>
                    We tabulate the first few squares and cubes and their residues, and we list what the tables show.
                </p>
            </abstract>
        </frontmatter>

        <section xml:id="section-tables">
            <title>The tables</title>

            <p>
                <xref ref="table-powers"/> gives <m>n^2</m> and <m>n^3</m> for <m>1 \leq n \leq 5</m>, and <xref ref="table-residues"/> reduces them modulo <m>4</m>.
            </p>

            <table xml:id="table-powers">
                <title>Squares and cubes</title>
                <tabular halign="right" top="medium" bottom="medium">
                    <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>n</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>n^2</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>n^3</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>1</cell>
                        <cell>1</cell>
                        <cell>1</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>2</cell>
                        <cell>4</cell>
                        <cell>8</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>3</cell>
                        <cell>9</cell>
                        <cell>27</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>4</cell>
                        <cell>16</cell>
                        <cell>64</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>5</cell>
                        <cell>25</cell>
                        <cell>125</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </table>

            <table xml:id="table-residues">
                <title>Residues modulo <m>4</m></title>
                <tabular top="medium" bottom="medium">
                    <col halign="left"/>
                    <col halign="center"/>
                    <col halign="center"/>
                    <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
                        <cell>parity of <m>n</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>n^2 \bmod 4</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>n^3 \bmod 4</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>even</cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>odd, <m>n \equiv 1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>1</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>odd, <m>n \equiv 3</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>3</m></cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </table>
        </section>

        <section xml:id="section-observations">
            <title>What the tables show</title>

            <p>
                Three things can be read from <xref ref="table-residues"/>.
                <ol>
                    <li xml:id="item-square-residues">
                        <p>
                            A square is congruent to <m>0</m> or <m>1</m> modulo <m>4</m>.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li xml:id="item-cube-residues">
                        <p>
                            A cube takes three of the four residues:
                            <ul>
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                        <m>0</m>, from the even integers;
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <p>
                                        <m>1</m> and <m>3</m>, from the odd ones.
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            No cube is congruent to <m>2</m> modulo <m>4</m>.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                The first of these, <xref ref="item-square-residues"/>, is the one used most often.
            </p>

            <p>
                We use two words in a fixed sense.
                <dl>
                    <li>
                        <title>Residue</title>
                        <p>
                            The remainder on division by the modulus, taken in <m>\{0, 1, \dots, m - 1\}</m>.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <title>Small case</title>
                        <p>
                            A value of <m>n</m> for which the computation fits in <xref ref="table-powers"/>.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </dl>
            </p>
        </section>
    </article>
</pretext>
